  "why": "The paper demonstrates a successful safeguard bypass but does not specifically design its fuzzing method to achieve this. In a case study, the authors create a defended model through adversarial retraining, using images generated by their tool, HDTest. This retrained model acts as a safeguard. They then attack this defended model with a new set of adversarial images. The results show that while the attack success rate drops, it is not eliminated, meaning the attacks can still bypass the safeguard. This constitutes a demonstration of a safeguard bypass. However, the design of HDTest itself—its failure oracle (misprediction) and its guidance mechanism (distance between hypervectors)—is not tailored to bypassing defenses. The fuzzer is simply applied to a defended model without any modification to its core logic, fitting the criteria for a 'Medium' rating.",
